# L §2.1 "A four-digit literal is a year where a period is expected and an integer in an integer index"; in
# `x - 1000` with x money no period is expected, so 1000 is a figure and L §7.1's literal rule refuses it in a def
# (`LOAD-LITERAL`), as it refuses `x - 500` (fault, writer 7: it was refused LOAD-UNIT as `money DUK and year4`).
=== f.tally
model f
  tally 2
  on 2025-01-01
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
input x: money DUK
def y: money DUK = x - 1000
ask q: y
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LITERAL figure 1000 in a rule; make it a row (f.tally:8)
